\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
While kCELL exhibits a higher prequential error during the learning phase,
 its final performance on the test set is superior to the other algorithms.
 The steady decrease in error indicates that the ensemble of local expert agents is effectively organizing into a meaninful representation of the inverse dynamics as the agent population tend to stabilize.
 The fact that kCELL achieves a lower MAE than the other algorithms earlier than it does for RMSE suggests that,
 while kCELL is highly accurate on average,
 its performance is affected by occasional large errors,
 to which RMSE is more sensitive.
\end_layout

