It can be noted that R-tree maintains a competitive edge in low-dimensional regimes (
\begin_inset Formula $n\leq5$
\end_inset

).
 Indeed,
 R-trees struggle in higher dimensions due to the curse of dimensionality.
 In higher dimensional regimes the distinction between nearest and farthest points becomes meaningless due to distance stretching and pruning becomes ineffective 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "kouiroukidis2011effects"
literal "false"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
However,
 the performances of the R-tree compared to GPU does not seem monotonic.
 In Figures 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
