\begin_layout Paragraph
Prequential Error Analysis
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
As shown both in Table 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "tab:gpCELL-Stationary-Results"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"

\end_inset

 and Figure 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "fig:Evolution-of-Prequential-gpCELL"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"

\end_inset

 (illustrates the evolution of the prequential error during learning),
 gpCELL exhibits a higher prequential error than kCELL,
 Mondrian Forests and LWPR throughout the majority of the experiment.
 This gap in immediate adaptation capability could be explained by the behavior of GPs in unexplored regions.
 As the kernel covariance decays with distance,
 GP predictions revert to the constant prior mean.
 This can lead to higher errors on Out-of-Distribution (OoD) points before the input space is fully covered by local expert agents.
\end_layout

