\begin_layout Paragraph
Synthesis
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The results of this comparative study validate empirically the gpCELL algorithm learning capabilities.
 Validating the integration of another type of learning model for the design of a CELL learning algorithm.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The key takeaways from this experiment can be summarized as follows:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Non-Linear Representations
\series default
:
 gpCELL results in more accurate representation of the underlying function (lowest final MAE).
 However,
 this comes at the cost of a slower adpatation and higher errors on OoD inputs.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Uncertainty
\series default
:
 gpCELL provides a well-calibrated predictive variance (95% PICP) which quantifies the reliability of predictions.
 It provides a complementary measure of uncertainty that lies in the output space instead of the input space,
 as is the case for epistemic uncertainty estimation through the spatial organization of local expert agents.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Population Overgrowth
\series default
:
 Contrary to what was intended,
 the transition to non-linear internal models did not naturally lead to a more parsimonious population.
 Because gpCELL created more agents than kCELL despite using the same spatialization hyperparameters suggests that the current learning rules under the hyperparameters used leads to an overgrowth of agents compared to their individual modeling capabilities.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
While gpCELL is more computationally demanding and memory intensive than kCELL,
 the reliability of uncertainty quantification introduced by the use of local GPs makes it a promising candidate for safe control tasks.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Note Note
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Overall,
 these results show that gpCELL provides a more accurate representation of complex robot dynamics (lowest final MAE) while providing well calibrated confidence intervals on predictions (95% PICP).
 The predictive variance provides a complementary measure of epistemic uncertainty in the output space to the spatial organization of agents in the input space.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
While gpCELL is more computationally demanding and memory-intensive than kCELL,
 the reliability of uncertainty quantification makes it a promising candidate for safe control tasks.
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

