nolink "false"

\end_inset

,
 the speed recommendation problem could be abstracted as a Human-Robot Collaboration (HRC) problem.
 This shift in perspective allowed to break down the speed recommendation problem into two sub-problems:
 the accurate modeling of the vehicle future movements when driven by a human driver and the safe exploitation of this model to provide recommendations.
 The relationship between HRC and Speed Recommendation is illustrated in Figure 
