caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"

\end_inset

.
 Having layed out these theoretical and algorithmic foundations,
 this chapter returns to the initial motivation of this thesis work:
 speed recommendation.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The goal of this chapter is to provide an industrial perspective on the progress of works towards safe and efficient intelligent speed recommendation systems and how the works of this thesis on HRC contributed to this progress.
 While the preceding chapters established the promising aspect of the CELL instantiations,
 real-world integration within the automotive sector requires addressing a broader set of requirements,
 ranging from multi-objective optimization to certifiability.
 We argue that the intrinsic properties of the CELL instantiations,
 specifically the spatialized local knowledge representation through local expert agents and the introspection capabilities,
 position this type of models as an interesting research topic for bridging the gap between personalized online learning and safety-critical industrial standards.
\end_layout

